RF.put("questb:b1",{"8801":{"id":8801,"t":"C'Thun's Legacy","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Eye of C'Thun to Caelastrasz in the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj.\nEye of C'Thun C'Thun in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\nProvided: Eye of C'Thun","desc":"The walls of Ahn'Qiraj tremble. A force of evil, older than the world itself, has been destroyed.\nAs you look at the remnants of the colossal abomination your heart nearly freezes. Even in death you can feel the legacy of C'Thun's evil around you.\nYou have done what was thought to be impossible.\nYou grab at an eye stalk of the fiend, stowing it safely in your pack.\nTake the Eye of C'Thun to the dragons in the next chamber.","rew":"Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Cenarion Circle\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"<Caelastrasz kneels before you.>\nLord ‹name›, you have freed us of its grasp.","done":"We will leave this place on our own, Lord ‹name› - once we are certain that the evil within has been wholly destroyed. Your journey of legend is almost at an end.\nStart an item: Eye of C'Thun End Caelestrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Shareable No Quest ID 8801\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 19,900 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] C'Thun's Legacy this quest\nTake the Eye of C'Thun to Caelastrasz in the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj.\nEye of C'Thun\n9,950 XP\n2 [ 60 ] The Savior of Kalimdor\nTake the Eye of C'Thun to Anachronos at the Caverns of Time.\nCaelestrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8561":{"id":8561,"t":"Conqueror's Crown","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Vek'nilash's Circlet, 2 Idols of the Sun, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nVek'nilash's Circlet Emperor Vek'nilash in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of the Sun Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Crystal Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Stone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 3000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"The Twin Emperors... their incessant whispers are slowly taking a toll on my sanity. They mock me, knowing I cannot step further into their domain to save my brother Arygos.\nIn my visions I see their monstrous faces adorned by powerful crowns. But I will have my revenge... I will transmute these symbols of Qiraji power to ones better suited to our needs.\nBring me the components I require, ‹name›. I will give you a headpiece of unmatched power.","rew":"You will receive:\nConqueror's Crown\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Did you bring me the components I asked for, ‹name›?","done":"You've succeeded! The whispers from the Twin Emperors have ceased.\nTake this as a reward. The mere sight of it will strike fear in the hearts of the Qiraji... it shall remind them of their fallen leaders and of the mortal that slew them.\nStart Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Warrior Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8561\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Conqueror's Crown this quest\nBring Vek'nilash's Circlet, 2 Idols of the Sun, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj.\nAndorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8641":{"id":8641,"t":"Deathdealer's Spaulders","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,950, 0.66 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Qiraji Bindings of Command, 2 Idols of the Sun, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Neutral reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nQiraji Bindings of Command Viscidus in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Princess Huhuran in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of the Sun Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Silver Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Clay Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 0 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"It is said among us that the ornate shoulder armor worn by the mortal races started as an attempt to emulate the wings of a dragon.\nBring me the bindings worn by the highest Qiraji leaders and I shall shape them into a set of pauldrons more dreadful than even the wings of Nefarian himself!","rew":"You will receive:\nDeathdealer's Spaulders\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Have you collected the components I require?","done":"From the materials you bring and from the scales of our fallen Qiraji foes I make you these pauldrons, mortal. May they grant you the protection you need and may the sight of them strike fear into our enemies.\nStart Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Rogue Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8641\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 13,200 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Deathdealer's Spaulders this quest\nBring the Qiraji Bindings of Command, 2 Idols of the Sun, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj.\nAndorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"7281":{"id":7281,"t":"Brotherly Love","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel into Stormpike territory and slay Commander Karl Philips. Return to Commander Louis Philips when the task is complete.\nCommander Karl Philips slain in Alterac Valley","desc":"Tragic... My brother faces me on the field of battle: A commander for the Stormpike.\nOf the four Stormpike Commanders, he is undoubtedly the most dangerous. Perhaps if he is slain, the Banshee Queen could turn him as she did me - show him the error of his ways...\nDeep within enemy territory you will find my brother. Slay him and return to me. I trust that you are capable of completing this mission, soldier.\nAnd soldier, do not go alone.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Frostwolf Clan\n+100 reputation with Undercity\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"How it must pain him to remain as one of the living while his beloved brother has ascended to perfection.","done":"Your heroics will not go unnoticed, ‹name›.\nI must waste no time if he is to be saved. Sylvanas must be contacted!\nStart Commander Louis Philips End Commander Louis Philips Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Both factions Type PvP Shareable Yes Quest ID 7281","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"6881":{"id":6881,"t":"Ivus the Forest Lord","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Storm Crystal Winterax Warrior 80 % , Corporal Teeka Bloodsnarl 80 % , Alliance Sentinel 80 % , Stormpike Mountaineer 80 % and 4 more","back":"The Frostwolf Clan is protected by a taint of elemental energy. Their shaman meddle in powers that will surely destroy us all if left unchecked.\nThe damage has grown too great for the Circle to control! Ivus must be called to our aid.\nThe Frostwolf soldiers carry elemental charms called storm crystals. We can use the charms to conjure Ivus. Venture forth and claim the crystals, ‹name›!","done":"Well done, ‹name›. I will use the power of this charm to augment the magic that has already been gathered. When enough power has been amassed, I shall focus the collected energies and call upon the Forest Lord to aid our cause.\nStart Arch Druid Renferal Alterac Valley End Arch Druid Renferal Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Alliance Type PvP Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6881","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"6801":{"id":6801,"t":"Lokholar the Ice Lord","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Stormpike Soldier's Blood Winterax Mystic , Syndicate Agent , Syndicate Brigand , Alliance Sentinel and 4 more","back":"I come from Thunder Bluff, ‹race›. Cairne himself has seen to it that I assist the Frostwolf Clan in these dire times.\nBut let us not waste any more time. You must strike down our enemies and bring to me their blood. Once enough blood has been gathered, the ritual of summoning may begin.\nVictory will be assured when the elemental lord is loosed upon the Stormpike army.","done":"The blood of our enemies has been shed. I shall mix this blood with the rest that has been gathered. Once the offering is complete, the Ice Lord shall show these Stormpike dogs the full wrath of the Frostwolf Clan!\nStart Primalist Thurloga Alterac Valley End Primalist Thurloga Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Horde Type PvP Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6801","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7121":{"id":7121,"t":"The Quartermaster","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with the Stormpike Quartermaster.","desc":"‹name›, our quartermaster charged me to direct new recruits to him. He needs supplies from caches stored in the mines of Alterac, and he'll probably send you to get them.\nFollow the road. You'll find our quartermaster to the west.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+10 reputation with Stormpike Guard\n+10 reputation with Ironforge","done":"It's good to see fresh troops here, ‹name›, but with a little luck you'll get into some action and won't be fresh for long!\nSpeak with me again. I have tasks I must discuss with you....\nStart Mountaineer Boombellow Alterac Valley End Stormpike Quartermaster Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Alliance Type PvP Shareable Yes Quest ID 7121","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"8161":{"id":8161,"t":"Cut Arathor Supply Lines","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,750 experience instead of 3,300, 0.83 times as much.","obj":"Win the battle for Arathi Basin, get an Arathi Resource Crate, and return it to Deathstalker Mortis at Hammerfall.\nArathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"The League of Arathor is sparing no expense in their move to retake Arathi. They, and all the races of the Alliance, now stream to this distant region, intent on expanding their hold from Refuge Pointe. We must stop them, and the best means to stop them is to take their supplies.\nYou can help us, ‹name›. Enter Arathi Basin, known for its rich mines, fertile land and skilled craftsman. Capture and control every base you can, win the battle, and return to me with the resources you gain.","rew":"Money: 1 10 1 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,750\n+200 reputation with The Defilers\nLevel 35 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 31 33 38 44 Side Horde Type PvP Shareable No Quest ID 8161","cats":["arathi-basin"]},"641":{"id":641,"t":"Sigil of Thoradin","lv":40,"min":32,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the restored Sigil of Thoradin to Zengu in Hammerfall.\nSigil of Thoradin\nProvided: Sigil of Thoradin","desc":"The reconstruction worked flawlessly. The sigil can now be used to unlock the seal on Trollbane's tomb. Return it to Zengu, no doubt he has additional tasks for you to complete.","rew":"Experience: 320\n+25 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"‹name›! Do you have the second sigil?","done":"We're halfway to being able to remove Trol'kalar from Trollbane's tomb. We are not exactly sure where the third sigil is, as its holders seem to move around Arathi quite a bit, but I have faith that you'll be able to find it.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":74.7,"y":36.3,"n":"Tor'gan","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.8,"y":34,"n":"Zengu","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"6641":{"id":6641,"t":"Vorsha the Lasher","lv":23,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Keep Muglash safe as he travels to the brazier. Help him by putting the brazier out, then protect him as you fight against the Naga.\nIf you are successful, return to the Zoram'gar Outpost and inform the Warsong Runner of the death of Vorsha the Lasher.","desc":"Vorsha the Lasher... the fiendish hydra that roams the seas...\nShe has attacked our outpost, each time unprovoked, laying waste to anything that falls in her path.\nBut I am ready, ‹name›. I have prepared to best the hydra and end these attacks on Zoram'gar.\nThe naga honor the wicked nature of this beast with a brazier that remains lit on an island just off the coast. I believe that if we put it out, Vorsha will appear in anger.\nWe will need help, so be sure to bring some strong allies.","rew":"You will receive:\nHorn Ring\nExperience: 2,300","done":"I have witnessed many naga attacks since I arrived here. It puts my mind at ease that Vorsha will no longer roam freely.\nWe are in your debt, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":12.1,"y":34.6,"n":"Muglash","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":12.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Warsong Runner","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"1041":{"id":1041,"t":"The Caravan Road","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Clerk Daltry in Darkshire.","desc":"Turns out I was wrong about you, and that isn't something that happens everyday.\nIt just so happens that I remember this Velinde you're looking for. Isn't every day that a night elf priestess that wants to travel with a dirty old--but great for your shipping needs!--caravan like my own.\nWe split up on the way north, she was headed for Darkshire. The clerk there keeps all sorts of records. Might know something useful.\nBe careful in the jungle, it is a deadly place even at the best of times.","rew":"Experience: 1,200\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","done":"With all the strange happenings of the last few years, I keep as good records of strangers as I can. Never know when it might come in handy... though it's usually not pleasant business when it does. Not to suggest anything about this Velinde you're looking for.\nStranglethorn Vale Duskwood","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.4,"y":74.1,"n":"Caravaneer Ruzzgot","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":72.5,"y":46.9,"n":"Clerk Daltry","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"3601":{"id":3601,"t":"Kim'jael Indeed!","lv":53,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Search the Thalassian Base Camp for Kim'jael's Compass, Scope, Stuffed Chicken and Wizzlegoober, then return them to him in Azshara.\nKim'Jael's Compass Kim'jael's Equipment 25 %\nKim'Jael's Scope Kim'jael's Equipment 25 %\nKim'Jael's Stuffed Chicken Kim'jael's Equipment 25 %\nKim'Jael's Wizzlegoober Kim'jael's Equipment 25 %","desc":"Kim'jael indeed!! Do you know what Kim'jael means to the Blood elves, ‹name›? Little rat... or something like that. The big bullies!\nThey hired me to help them scout the area looking for some sort of lost treasures. Of course I jumped aboard the moment they said \"treasure\" and the amount they were willing to pay, but of course, they turned on me and tried to kill me... ME!\nGoes to show you, you can't trust a Blood elf.\nThe problem is, they still have my equipment and I can't get it back. Help me out?","rew":"You will receive:\n3 M73 Frag Grenade\nMoney: 8 0 gold, 8 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,550\n+150 reputation with Booty Bay\n-750 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Those stinkin' Blood elves. I tell ya, if I was as strong as you are, I'd go down there and teach them a thing or two myself! But I'll have to settle with payin' you to take care of 'em for me.","done":"Haha! You got them good, didn't you?!\nThis is great! That'll teach those Blood elves to betray their partners... especially someone as loyal as a goblin merchant! Bah, Blood elves...!\nWell, the least I can do for you is pay you for your time... just like I said I would.\nHere you go... those should be useful.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":53.5,"y":21.8,"n":"Kim'jael","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"6561":{"id":6561,"t":"Blackfathom Villainy","lv":27,"min":18,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 7,850 experience instead of 1,700, 4.62 times as much. New rewards: Dark Ritual Leggings, Cultist's Armguards. Read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeo","obj":"Bring the head of Twilight Lord Kelris to Bashana Runetotem in Thunder Bluff.\nHead of Kelris Twilight Lord Kelris","desc":"Strength has left me. Your help is needed!\nLong ago this site was a great temple of Elune. But misfortune led to ruin when the corruption of an Old God seeped up from beneath the earth and tainted the sacred Moon Well.\nAku'Mai, servant of the Old God, rose from the waters.\nThe Twilight's Hammer cultists have allied with the naga to occupy these grounds. The cultists, led by Kelris, sacrifice innocents to Aku'Mai for power.\nSlay Kelris and bring his head to Bashana in Thunder Bluff, ‹name›, please.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGravestone Scepter Arctic Buckler Dark Ritual Leggings Cultist's Armguards\nNew in Forever: Dark Ritual Leggings, Cultist's Armguards.\nMoney: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 7,850\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn\n+200 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"May the Earthmother be with you, ‹name›.\nPeace between the earth and all her people should be our goal. She has a grand plan for nature, and we all have a role to play in that plan.","done":"Kelris has eluded the Argent Dawn for some time.\nFor some time they considered him dead or missing.\nBy ending his reign you have spared the lives of many innocent people, ‹name›.\nEarthmother be praised! To sacrifice another to a servant of an Old God for personal gain is beyond disgusting!\nYou have done a great thing this day. Kelris was a creature of evil and sought to bring the world back to a time of chaos by worshipping such creatures as the Old Gods. Thank you, ‹name›.\nThunder Bluff Ashenvale","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":71.1,"y":34.2,"n":"Bashana Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["blackfathom-deeps"]},"4081":{"id":4081,"t":"KILL ON SIGHT: Dark Iron Dwarves","lv":52,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Venture to Blackrock Depths and destroy the vile aggressors!\nWarlord Goretooth wants you to kill 15 Anvilrage Guardsmen, 10 Anvilrage Wardens and 5 Anvilrage Footmen. Return to him once your task is complete.\nAnvilrage Guardsman slain : 0/ 15\nAnvilrage Warden slain : 0/ 10\nAnvilrage Footman slain : 0/ 5","desc":"By order of Warlord Goretooth, commander of the Kargath Expeditionary Force:\nAny and all of General Angerforge's forces within Blackrock Depths must be annihilated.\nAngerforge's men are ruthless killers, responsible for the mass murder of the 109th division of the Kargath Expeditionary Force. Heroes are warned to exercise extreme caution when confronting these brutes.\nAny person who destroys the first line of General Angerforge's forces in Blackrock Depths shall receive a tribute.","rew":"Money: 1 55 1 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,100\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"What is it, ‹race›? Can't you see I have a platoon to command?","done":"This first strike should put a crease in Angerforge's pants. Now, move along soldier. I have work to complete, battles to plan, enemies to crush!\nCheck the wanted signs for more work.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":3.7,"y":47.4,"n":"WANTED","s":1},{"z":"Badlands","x":5.8,"y":47.5,"n":"Warlord Goretooth","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4241":{"id":4241,"t":"Marshal Windsor","lv":54,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Blackrock Mountain in the northwest and enter Blackrock Depths. Find out what became of Marshal Windsor.\nYou recall Ragged John talking about Windsor being dragged off to a prison.","desc":"So that good for nothing coward says that Windsor is alive, eh?\nSuit up, deputy, you are going in to find him. If Windsor is alive, you are to bring him back. If he's dead, I want proof.\n<Maxwell laughs.>\nI bet you are getting tired of hearing that, aren't you?","rew":"Experience: 5,450\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Where is he! I'll murder him!","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":84.7,"y":69,"n":"Marshal Maxwell","s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"7201":{"id":7201,"t":"The Last Element","lv":54,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Blackrock Depths and recover 10 Essence of the Elements. Your first inclination is to search the golems and golem makers. You remember Vivian Lagrave also muttering something about elementals.\n10 Essence of the Elements Scald , Molten War Golem 80 % , Ragereaver Golem 80 % , Warbringer Construct 80 % and 4 more","desc":"There is work to be had for those venturing into the depths, ‹name›.\nThe Dark Irons have mastered creation of extremely powerful golems.\nInitial reports from our spies indicate that the dwarves use a unique power source to give their creations incomparable killing power.\nJust imagine what we could do with our abominations if we could get our hands on this essence of the elements! Turn that city upside down if you must, but do not return until you have found the essence! Payment will be worth the risk.","rew":"You will receive:\nLagrave's Seal\nMoney: 2 45 2 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,450\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Show them to me!","done":"Wonderful! I will have these sent by courier to the Undercity at once!\nAs for you - here is payment, as promised. Keep the change, you filthy beast!","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":2.9,"y":47.8,"n":"Shadowmage Vivian Lagrave","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4001":{"id":4001,"t":"What Is Going On?","lv":54,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,800 experience instead of 550, 12.36 times as much.","obj":"Speak with Kharan Mighthammer and gather information about Princess Moira Bronzebeard's kidnapping. Take that information to Thrall in Orgrimmar.\nYou recall Gor'shak mentioning that Kharan is being held in a cell nearby.","desc":"So far, my communication with the dwarf, Kharan, in the cell across the hall, has been limited. I have, however, managed to convince him that I, rather -we- mean him no harm.\nGo speak with him and gather as much information about the Princess and her captors as possible. Take that information back to the Warchief.\nThrall does not want the Princess harmed, but instead, has some grand plan laid out, which includes her being safely returned to Ironforge. Kharan already knows all of this... Go!","rew":"Experience: 6,800\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"What brings you to these hallowed grounds?","done":"This is a chance for the Horde to change the political climate of our war torn world forever. Listen carefully, ‹name›.\nFailure of this mission is not an option.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.7,"y":37.8,"n":"Thrall","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"8961":{"id":8961,"t":"Three Kings of Flame","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather the Incendicite of Incendius, the Ember of Emberseer and the Cinder of Cynders, along with a Hallowed Brazier, and return them to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain.\nIncendicite of Incendius Lord Incendius\nEmber of Emberseer Pyroguard Emberseer\nCinder of Cynders The Duke of Cynders\nHallowed Brazier","desc":"In order to summon Lord Valthalak we're first going to need to gather the other two-thirds of the amulet. To do that we need to get a brazier and some special coals to burn in it.\nThere are three nobles of fire, Lord Incedius in Blackrock Depths, Pyroguard Emberseer in Blackrock Spire and The Duke of Cynders in Silithus, with what we need. Collect from each a piece of their remains, and then return to me with a Hallowed Brazier, which can be purchased from the Argent Dawn if you are honored by them.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"It was our folly... our doom that we took that last job. If only we hadn't inadvertently stolen Lord Valthalak's spirit, which was contained in the amulet; if only there weren't those in our mercenary group that had been so greedy and divided it up amongst themselves. I'd be alive today, maybe tossing back a beer, or tossing one of my kids into the air.\n‹name›, don't let the avarice of the ignoble in our old mercenary company be your doom as well.","done":"I'm impressed, ‹class›, but there's no time to lose. I will give you your next task, because you will still need to acquire a few more important components before we can proceed.\nSpeak to me again when you feel that you are ready for the challenge that lies ahead.\nBurning Steppes Eastern Plaguelands Western Plaguelands Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-mountain"]},"7761":{"id":7761,"t":"Blackhand's Command","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"That is one stupid orc. It would appear as if you need to find this brand and gain the Mark of Drakkisath in order to access the Orb of Command.\nThe letter indicates that General Drakkisath guards the brand. Perhaps you should investigate.","desc":"Imbecile,\nI hold very little faith in your ability to prevent outsiders from accessing the master's lair. In the very likely event of your death, this orb has its own failsafe built in to prevent outsiders from teleporting directly into Blackwing.\nOnly those with the Mark of Drakkisath branded upon their hand may make use of this orb. Thankfully, Drakkisath is not nearly as incompetent as you, Quartermaster. He guards the brand himself!\n-Warchief Rend Blackhand\nP.S. Destroy this letter, idiot.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","done":"You don't even flinch as the smoldering brand is pressed into your flesh. You are so tough!\nYou now hold the Mark of Drakkisath. Have fun storming the castle.\nStart an item: Blackhand's Command End Drakkisath's Brand Level 60 , requires level 55 Difficulty 55 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 7761","cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"2801":{"id":2801,"t":"A Tale of Sorrow","lv":57,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Listen to the Fallen Hero of the Horde tell his story.","desc":"Before we may continue, you must hear my story.","rew":"Experience: 600","back":"Listen to what I have to say, ‹name›.","done":"The time to act is now, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":34.3,"y":66.1,"n":"Fallen Hero of the Horde","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"2721":{"id":2721,"t":"Kirith","lv":58,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find out what became of Lieutenant Kirith.","desc":"As one chapter of your adventure closes, another one begins, ‹name›.\nOne of my men is still unaccounted for, lost somewhere in the Blasted Lands. I am talking about Lieutenant Kirith, of course.\nAs I had mentioned earlier, we were both imprisoned and tortured by Allistarj, but poor Kirith, his strength of will faltered. I could hear the experiments from my cage; the tortured screams rang through the halls of the cave. That was the last I saw or heard of Kirith.","rew":"Experience: 6,200","done":"Trebor? Trebor sent you?","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":34.3,"y":66.1,"n":"Fallen Hero of the Horde","s":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"4481":{"id":4481,"t":"Libram of Constitution","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -30g instead of 0.","obj":"Black Diamond Borer Beetle 5.2 % , Dark Keeper Uggel 4.6 % , Crest Killer 3.8 % , Burrowing Thundersnout 3.6 % and 4 more\nLung Juice Cocktail\nLibram of Constitution Coldmine Guard 1.8 % in Alterac Valley , Ragepaw 0.3 % , Coldmine Miner 0.3 % in Alterac Valley , Hakkari Oracle 0.3 % and 4 more\n4 Night Dragon's Breath","rew":"You will receive:\nLesser Arcanum of Constitution","back":"There is a price to pay for all things in this world. The price for the specific item that you seek is thirty gold pieces.\nNaturally, I shall retain the majority of the components which you collected. But worry not, you shall have your trinket.","done":"It is disgrace to his memory... a mortal, such as yourself, finishing his life's work.\nTake your amalgamation and be gone!","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":65,"y":23.6,"n":"Mathredis Firestar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"97921":{"id":97921,"t":"Camping 101 herbalism","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Herbalist Pomeroy in Elwynn Forest to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your herbalism skill to 20","desc":"Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Incense Candle. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":44.8,"y":63.2,"n":"Sam Sarsaparilla","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":39.8,"y":48.4,"n":"Herbalist Pomeroy","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"4161":{"id":4161,"t":"Recipe of the Kaldorei","lv":7,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 7 Small Spider Legs for Zarrin in Dolanaar.\n7 Small Spider Leg Mother Fang 96.8 % , Mist Creeper 71 % , Wood Lurker 70.6 % , Moss Stalker 69.2 % and 4 more","desc":"Long ago, the night elves were called the kaldorei, a name that means \"children of the stars.\" Learning of the past is an important step in your path as a ‹class›, ‹name›, so listen well to what I have to tell you.\nThe kaldorei have always taken much pride in their harmonious relationship with nature. This means that we only take from nature what is necessary, and that we return in kind. This balance has afforded us much, ‹name›.\nGo out and collect seven small spider legs -- no more than that, and return to me.","rew":"You will receive:\nRecipe: Kaldorei Spider Kabob 3 Kaldorei Spider Kabob\nMoney: 85 0 gold, 0 silver, 85 copper Experience: 625\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Remember the balance, ‹name›. I wish you to develop an understanding and a strong empathy for the living forests.","done":"Always remember what I have shown you today, ‹name›. You are part of the balance that the night elves strive to keep intact, even during troublesome times.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.1,"y":61.3,"n":"Zarrin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["cooking"]},"94241":{"id":94241,"t":"Craftsmans writ dark leather tunic","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Dark Leather Tunic\nDark Leather Tunic","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Dark Leather Tunic, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"WHAT???","done":"Oh your timing is impeccable!\nCallahan! Your new shirt arrived. Hurry up and change so I can stop hearing about how itchy you are all the time.\nAnd for you, ‹race›. Here is your payment. Before you wander off, you should take a look at my wares now that you can afford 'em!","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":81.8,"y":19.8,"n":"Kzixx","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"94321":{"id":94321,"t":"Craftsmans writ flask of chromatic resistance","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Flask of Chromatic Resistance\nFlask of Chromatic Resistance","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Flask of Chromatic Resistance, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Flask of Chromatic Resistance Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94321","cats":["crafting"]},"961":{"id":961,"t":"Onu is meditating","lv":1,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Onu is meditating.","rew":"You will receive:\nPhial of Scrying","done":"The finding of Twilight's Hammer cultists is troubling. I must meditate on their intentions...\nWhen you have more information, speak to me through a scrying bowl. If you require a phial of scrying in order to create a bowl, then...here is another.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":43.6,"y":76.3,"n":"Onu","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":43.6,"y":76.4,"n":"Onu","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"1361":{"id":1361,"t":"Regthar Deathgate","lv":32,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Regthar Deathgate.","desc":"A warrior of the Horde, Regthar Deathgate, is recruiting agents for a mission into the land of Desolace. Speak with him if you wish to volunteer. He is stationed in the Barrens, in a series of bunkers west of the Crossroads.\nAnd sharpen your weapons. Desolace is a place torn by war.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+25 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"Yes, I am recruiting. This mission leads into Desolace, against the centaur there. I will be brief so that you may quickly begin.\nHillsbrad Foothills The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":63.2,"y":20.7,"n":"Krusk","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":45.3,"y":28.4,"n":"Regthar Deathgate","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"6161":{"id":6161,"t":"Claim Rackmore's Treasure!","lv":36,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Rackmore's Silver Key. Find Rackmore's Golden Key. Find and open Rackmore's Chest.\nRackmore's Silver Key Drysnap Pincer 15 % , Drysnap Crawler 15 %\nRackmore's Golden Key Slitherblade Sea Witch 55 % , Slitherblade Oracle 55 % , Slitherblade Tidehunter 55 % , Slitherblade Razortail 55 % and 4 more","desc":"Rackmore's log tells of how his ship was sailing for Feathermoon Stronghold when it was attacked by seafaring creatures. To prevent his treasure from falling into enemy hands, he hid his chest on Ranazjar Isle.\nTo open the chest requires two keys, a silver and a gold. These keys were lost, but if the keys and the chest are found, a treasure awaits!","rew":"You will receive:\nCaptain Rackmore's Wheel Captain Rackmore's Tiller\nMoney: 1 15 1 gold, 15 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,800","back":"This chest is securely locked.","done":"Chest opens to reveal Rackmore's treasure!","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":36.1,"y":30.4,"n":"Rackmore's Log","s":1},{"z":"Desolace","x":30,"y":8.7,"n":"Rackmore's Chest","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"7441":{"id":7441,"t":"Pusillin and the Elder Azj'Tordin","lv":58,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Dire Maul and locate the Imp, Pusillin. Convince Pusillin to give you Azj'Tordin's Book of Incantations through any means necessary.\nReturn to Azj'Tordin at the Lariss Pavilion in Feralas should you recover the Book of Incantations.\nBook of Incantations Pusillin","desc":"I had let my guard down for only one moment, stranger. In my haste to escape the grip of the fallen Prince, I was robbed. A most foul demon, the imp Pusillin, pilfered my book of incantations and the key to the once great halls of Eldre'Thalas.\nI no longer hold interest in the key, as I have exchanged my immortality for freedom, but I desperately need my book of incantations.\nFind the imp, Pusillin, and recover my book.\nSearch the Warpwood Quarter of Dire Maul for Pusillin.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSpry Boots Sprinter's Sword\nMoney: 1 75 1 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 7,750\n+200 reputation with Shen'dralar","back":"I regret nothing, stranger. The Queen has long since passed. The works of the Shen'Dralar have been marred by the madness of Prince Tortheldrin. I seek only freedom... Escape...","done":"You have found it! A curse upon that miserable imp. Alas, my material possessions are meager at best. You may choose from what I have to offer.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":76.9,"y":37.4,"n":"Azj'Tordin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dire-maul"]},"6001":{"id":6001,"t":"Body and Heart","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Cenarion Moondust on the Moonkin Stone of Auberdine to bring forth Lunaclaw. From there, you must face Lunaclaw and earn the strength of body and heart it possesses.\nSpeak with Mathrengyl Bearwalker in Darnassus when you are done.\nProvided: Cenarion Moondust","desc":"Directly east of Auberdine lay many moonkin caves. The one closest to Auberdine has a Moonkin Stone inside it. Lunaclaw, the defender of the stone, will face you only when Cenarion Moondust is applied to it. Lunaclaw possesses within it a strength that you must use as one of the Claw.\nYou've earned the right to use this Cenarion Moondust, ‹name›... now show me that you've earned the right to possess the strength of body and the strength of heart needed as a druid!","rew":"Experience: 850\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"You have finally taken your large step into a much larger world, ‹name›. I sense the teaching of the Great Bear Spirit within you, and I sense that you have received the strength that Lunaclaw possessed.\nThere are no further obstacles in your way... let me now teach you what it means to be a Druid of the Claw!\nDarnassus Darkshore","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":35.4,"y":8.4,"n":"Mathrengyl Bearwalker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"5921":{"id":5921,"t":"Moonglade","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the spell \"Teleport: Moonglade\" to travel to Moonglade. When you arrive, speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven.","desc":"All druids are welcome in the sacred lands of Moonglade, regardless of the current tensions in the Cenarion Circle between Arch Druid Staghelm and Keeper Remulos - Moonglade's guardian. Now that you're learning the ways of the Claw, I'll teach you the spell that lets you transport yourself there. Cast it whenever you seek Moonglade's knowledge or solace.\nAs for your first lesson, travel to Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven about the path you're now on. Good luck, young druid.","rew":"Experience: 210\n+25 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"\"And so it begins. Father Cenarius. And so it begins.\"\nDendrite makes a quick, invisible gesture in the air above him. A slight aura of power falls over him.\n\"The first perspective of nature you must adapt to is that of the bear. I will put you on the path to understanding this aspect of druidic life, but it is you that must embrace it and propagate it - now and forever!\"\nDarnassus Moonglade","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":35.4,"y":8.4,"n":"Mathrengyl Bearwalker","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.6,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"5841":{"id":5841,"t":"Welcome!","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Coldridge Valley Gift Voucher to Yori Crackhelm.\nColdridge Valley Gift Voucher\nProvided: Coldridge Valley Gift Voucher","desc":"Welcome to the World of Warcraft!\nAs special thanks for purchasing the World of Warcraft Collector's Edition, turn in this gift voucher to Yori Crackhelm in Coldridge Valley. You'll then be given a gift: a little companion to join you on your quest for adventure and glory.\nThanks again, and enjoy your stay in the World of Warcraft!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDiablo Stone Panda Collar Zergling Leash","back":"Hello! It is a pleasure to meet you!\nI see you have a special voucher. Give it to me and I will offer you something in exchange.","done":"You are indeed a special hero, ‹name›. We welcome you to the world of Azeroth, and offer you one of these unique gifts!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":30.1,"y":71.7,"n":"Yori Crackhelm","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"3361":{"id":3361,"t":"A Refugee's Quandary","lv":3,"min":3,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Felix's Box, Felix's Chest and Felix's Bucket of Bolts to Felix Whindlebolt in Anvilmar.\nFelix's Box Felix's Box\nFelix's Chest Felix's Chest\nFelix's Bucket of Bolts Felix's Bucket of Bolts","desc":"We drove the troggs out of Gnomeregan, but then it all went so horribly wrong! Now our home is completely irradiated, and we gnomes have been scattered all over Dun Morogh.\nIn my haste to get away from the radiation, I lost all my personal belongings and tools. It was the trolls that got them. They stole my chest, my box, and my bucket of bolts! They took them back to their camps southwest of Anvilmar.\nI'm no adventurer - could you find my things and bring them here to me, please?","rew":"Money: 50 0 gold, 0 silver, 50 copper Experience: 250\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Oh goodness ‹name›, this town is not well suited for the likes of me. There are as many nasty creatures here as there were in Gnomeregan before the accident!\nDo you have my belongings? If you don't, then who knows what the trolls have done with them now...","done":"Huzzah, you've found them! You're an absolute savior, my friend. Here, it's not much, but it's something for the trouble I've put you through! Thank you!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":28.5,"y":67.6,"n":"Felix Whindlebolt","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"98321":{"id":98321,"t":"Flintfires shipment","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 8 Flintfire Shipments from the Grizzled Den for Tongus Flintfire in Kharanos.\n8 Flintfire's Shipment","desc":"Hoha! Good to see a ‹race› who's not afraid to get their hands dirty.\nIf yer lookin' fer work, I'm afraid I'm a little short on supplies at the moment. Our most reliable source of ore has been overrun by wendigo and now the cave has been abandoned. The miners had to drop everything when they fled!\nSay, why don't ye poke yer head around the Grizzled Den to the west and see if you can find some of our missing shipments. It would save us a great deal o' trouble.","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 0 silver, 45 copper Experience: 625\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Wendigos are nasty beasties. Its just good all the miners made it out of the Grizzled Den in one piece!","done":"Now that's more like it! With these shipments we'll get the forge back up and runnin' in no time!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":45.2,"y":52,"n":"Tognus Flintfire","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"95041":{"id":95041,"t":"Data hoarders","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 7 Gnomeregan Archival Data cards from around Gnomeregan, then deliver them to Jemma Quikswitch in Ironforge.\n7 Gnomeregan Archival Data","desc":"Before we fled Gnomeregan, I made a hard copy of my family's archives. Arcanotechnical field equations, Second War submarine hull designs, Grandma Quikswitch's chili recipe... our greatest accomplishments are in those files.\nIt wasn't until we reached Ironforge that I found a hole in my pack! Several punch cards are gone, and without them the data's too scrambled to recover.\nThe cards must be buried in the snow, somewhere outside Gnomeregan. Could you find them? I know it's a long shot...","back":"How is the data retrieval progressing?","done":"These cards seem a bit damp... but I can work with this! Thank you, Archnatum!","pins":[{"z":"Ironforge","x":67.8,"y":43.8,"n":"Jemma Quikswitch","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"4641":{"id":4641,"t":"Your Place In The World","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Your Place In The World.","obj":"Speak with Gornek. You recall Kaltunk marking your map with his location and mentioning that Gornek resided in the Den, a building to the west.","desc":"Finally, you are of age, ‹name›... of age to battle in the name of the Horde. To conquer for the glory of the Warchief.\nYes...\n<Kaltunk looks you over.>\nYou will do nicely.\nNo doubt you wish to find a great dragon or demon and strangle it with your bare hands, but perhaps it would be wise to start on something less... dangerous.\n<Kaltunk laughs.>\nReport to Gornek, he should be able to assign a task better suited to a young ‹class›. You will find Gornek in the Den, to the west.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+50 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"The carapace of a scorpid isn't so thick that the strength of a determined ‹class› will be deterred. Strike strongly and without doubt, and the scorpids should prove easy prey.","done":"Another one of Kaltunk's recruits, hm?\nA sorry state of affairs we find ourselves in if this is the best the Horde can produce. No matter. By the time we think you're ready to leave the Valley, you'll be a proud ‹class› of the Horde.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":43.3,"y":68.5,"n":"Kaltunk","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":42.1,"y":68.3,"n":"Gornek","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"5441":{"id":5441,"t":"Lazy Peons","lv":4,"min":3,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Foreman's Blackjack on Lazy Peons when they're sleeping. Wake up 5 peons, then return the Foreman's Blackjack to Foreman Thazz'ril in the Valley of Trials.\nForeman's Blackjack\nPeons Awoken : 0/ 5\nProvided: Foreman's Blackjack","desc":"Cursed peons! They work hard gathering lumber from the trees of the valley, but they're always taking naps! I need someone to help keep the peons in line.\nYou look like the right ‹race› for my task. Here, you take this blackjack and use it on any lazy peons you find sleeping on the job. A good smack will get them right back to work! Return the blackjack when you're done.\nLousy slacking peons...","rew":"Experience: 450\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"No good lazy...\nEh? Do you have my blackjack? Did you catch any peons sleeping on the job?!","done":"Good, good. Maybe they'll think twice before slacking next time! Thanks for the help!","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":44.6,"y":68.7,"n":"Foreman Thazz'ril","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"2161":{"id":2161,"t":"A Peon's Burden","lv":5,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Ukor's Burden to Innkeeper Grosk in Razor Hill.\nUkor's Burden\nProvided: Ukor's Burden","desc":"Excuse me? Can you help me?\nI have a load of food here. I walked along the road and braved scorpids and spiders and worse! I brought the food to the Valley of Trials because I thought they needed it and I like to help out. But they don't need any food! Now I have to take it back to Razor Hill and I'm afraid of all the beasts along the way...\nCan you take it for me? I'm just a peon, but you're a hero. You fear nothing!\nTake it to Innkeeper Grosk at the Razor Hill inn. Thank you!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n5 Tough Hunk of Bread 5 Refreshing Spring Water\nExperience: 110\n+25 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+25 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Welcome to Razor Hill!","done":"Ah, this is the food Ukor brought to the Valley of Trials. Did they not need it? Well, I guess they like to starve you heroes in training. Builds spirit, they say!\nThank you for returning the food. I'll stick it back on the shelves... but here, let me offer you some refreshment first!\nAnd don't forget to rest here in the inn. You may be a brave ‹class› ready to take on the world, but if your energy is sapped you won't be doing yourself, or the Horde, much good.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":52.1,"y":68.3,"n":"Ukor","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":51.5,"y":41.6,"n":"Innkeeper Grosk","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"97281":{"id":97281,"t":"A simmering storm","lv":11,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Dull Stormy Orb to Rezlak near Drygulch Ravine.","desc":"<Before you is a strange orb and with a dull surface. When picked up a small electrical current seems to vibrate from within. Upon closer inspection, it looks as if a dark mist swirls within and every so often a small electrical spark can be seen.\nIt is clear the harpy was using it for some purpose. Perhaps Rezlak would be interested in this object?>","done":"Woah, where did you find a neat thing like that? Ya know it reminds me of the other thing my boss Gazlowe always used to tell me...","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":46.4,"y":23,"n":"Rezlak","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"321":{"id":321,"t":"Lightforge Iron","lv":29,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Search the wreckage of The Flying Osprey in the Wetlands.","desc":"The shipwrecks off the shore here are the doomed Third Fleet of Kul'Tiras, burned and sunk by Red Dragons during the last Great War.\nThe Fleet hailed from Lordaeron, but one ship, an Elvish Destroyer: Flying Osprey, was with it. It was shipping a load of Lightforge Iron and joined the Third Fleet for protection. Ironic that it sunk to the same dragons...\nEnough history. The Flying Osprey is wrecked to the south of Menethil Harbor. If you find the Lightforge Iron there, bring it to me.","rew":"You will receive:\nLightforge Ingot\nExperience: 600\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"This chest is waterlogged, and its siding broken. Many claw marks mar both the inside and outside of the chest...as if Murlocs have searched through it and stolen its treasure.\nBut tucked deep within the chest is a single Lightforge Ingot. Unfortunately, many more will be needed if enough metal to fashion a weapon is to be gained.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":10.6,"y":60.6,"n":"Glorin Steelbrow","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":12.1,"y":64.2,"n":"Waterlogged Chest","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"401":{"id":401,"t":"Wait for Sirra to Finish","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Wait a moment, then speak with Sirra Von'Indi again.","desc":"I'm almost finished translating that note. If you come back in a few moments I should be done.","rew":"Experience: 1,850","done":"There we are. It's translated...\n<The air grows heavy, as if a thick, black curtain is drawn over the land...>","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":72.6,"y":47.6,"n":"Sirra Von'Indi","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"1201":{"id":1201,"t":"Theramore Spies","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 9 Theramore Infiltrators, then return to Nazeer Bloodpike in Brackenwall Village.\nTheramore Infiltrator slain : 0/ 9","desc":"The Horde and Alliance hold an uneasy truce. Outlying skirmishes and covert actions are taken by one side against the other, and it is our duty to ensure the Horde is on top!\nNow is the chance to do just that.\nAlliance infiltrators have taken positions east of Brackenwall Village. They spy on the village and report our movements to Theramore, which we cannot allow.\nHunt down the infiltrators and slay them. Send a clear message to their superiors that we will not tolerate their spies' presence!","rew":"Experience: 2,750\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Did you find the infiltrators, ‹name›?","done":"Good work. Their infiltrators are skilled, but they're not good enough to escape the watchful eye of the Horde!","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":35.2,"y":30.7,"n":"Nazeer Bloodpike","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"5601":{"id":5601,"t":"Sister Pamela","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Pamela Redpath in Darrowshire.","desc":"I fled Lordaeron during the great war, and was lucky to escape before the Scourge swept through my homeland and turned it into a plagued nightmare! I was lucky, but my family was not. I fear they were all killed during the battle of Darrowshire.\nDarrowshire is a village in the Eastern Kingdoms, nestled in the southern hills of what is now the Eastern Plaguelands. Will you go there and search for my family? I miss them so much, especially my little sister Pamela.\nPlease, find her for me!","rew":"Experience: 550","done":"Where is my sister Jessica? She left so long ago, when I was just a little girl. She cried so much when she went away. I don't know why she cried! Maybe she fell and hit her toe.\nWhen Jessica was here we used to play games and dance and pick pretty flowers around the house. And sometimes we'd hide when we saw daddy coming home, then jump out and surprise him!\nCome back, Jessica! If you come back then maybe daddy will too and we can all play together again...\nWinterspring Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.3,"y":39,"n":"Jessica Redpath","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":31.2,"y":78,"n":"Pamela Redpath","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9201":{"id":9201,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Greater Arcane Protection Potion","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 15 Greater Arcane Protection Potions and the Craftsman's Writ - Greater Arcane Protection Potion - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Greater Arcane Protection Potion\n15 Greater Arcane Protection Potion\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Greater Arcane Protection Potion","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order AL-1420:\n15 Greater Arcane Protection Potions.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"<Packmaster Stonebruiser pops open one of the greater arcane protection potions and take a swig.>\nWOOT! These pack a kick, baby! A kick I say!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9121":{"id":9121,"t":"The Dread Citadel - Naxxramas","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -60g instead of 0.","obj":"Archmage Angela Dosantos at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 5 Arcane Crystals, 2 Nexus Crystals, 1 Righteous Orb and 60 gold pieces. You must also be Honored with the Argent Dawn.\n5 Arcane Crystal Hakkari Thorium Vein 5.8 % , Rich Thorium Vein 2.9 % , Ooze Covered Rich Thorium Vein 2.9 % , Small Thorium Vein 2.6 % and 4 more\n2 Nexus Crystal\nRighteous Orb Archivist Galford 18 % in Stratholme , Crimson Guardsman 9 % in Stratholme , Crimson Gallant 8 % in Stratholme , Crimson Defender 8 % in Stratholme and 4 more\nReach 9000 reputation with Argent Dawn","desc":"In the thick of Plaguewood lies the entrance to the dread citadel of Naxxramas. Previously, all attempts to enter had been stymied by the magical wards placed upon the rune portal. That is, until now.\nWe have devised a way to gain entry via arcane cloaking - an old cantrip of the Kirin Tor with a few modifications of my own. Since your dedication to the cause of the Dawn is somewhat lacking, ‹name›, the price will be high. You may decline and choose to return when you are revered or exalted for a discount.","rew":"+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"None have entered Naxxramas and lived to tell the tale.","done":"You will feel a slight tingle, ‹name›. That sensation means it's working. Once complete, you will be able to enter Naxxramas by stepping upon the rune portal in Plaguewood.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.7,"n":"Archmage Angela Dosantos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"5281":{"id":5281,"t":"The Restless Souls","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 6,850, 0.96 times as much.","obj":"Find Egan. You only know that he was last seen around Stratholme.","desc":"There are those that died tragically in the fall of Stratholme. Many took their own lives, opting to hurl themselves into the myriad flames of the smoldering city rather than become one of the Scourge.\nThey now walk the streets of Stratholme as restless spirits.\nWe must aid them, ‹name›!\nI have an associate named Egan who has been doing miraculous work with ghosts and souls. Seek him out. He walks the eastern Plaguelands, near Stratholme, testing his innovations.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","done":"Alen has finally found someone brave enough, eh?","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":69.9,"y":53.7,"n":"Caretaker Alen","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":11.4,"y":26.6,"n":"Egan","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"4401":{"id":4401,"t":"Corrupted Songflower","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a songflower plant. A pungent, unhealthy odor emanates from the plant. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply some Cenarion plant salve to the songflower. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":40.1,"y":44.3,"n":"Corrupted Songflower","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4721":{"id":4721,"t":"Wild Guardians","lv":59,"min":52,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Trull Failbane in Felwood wants you to hunt 10 Berserk Owlbeasts in Winterspring.\nBerserk Owlbeast slain : 0/ 10","desc":"Runners have returned from Winterspring with reports that there is a series of small caves in the southern area of Winterspring. It seems that there are wildkin situated in the area around these caves. If there is something valuable that they are guarding, I believe that this is the place we will find it.\nYou will find these to be more of a challenge than the previous types, ‹name›. The creatures seem to have gone mad from exposure to the very thing that they strive to protect.","rew":"Money: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,400\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"You know your orders, ‹name›.","done":"Hard work is something I have great respect for, ‹name›. Now we can move forward with our plans for Winterspring.\nFelwood Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":34.7,"y":52.8,"n":"Trull Failbane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"8481":{"id":8481,"t":"The Root of All Evil","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Plant the Demon Summoning Torch in the mouth of High Chief Winterfall's cave in the Winterfall furbolg village. Defeat the demon and retrieve the Essence of Xandivious for Gorn One Eye in Timbermaw Hold.\nDemon Summoning Torch\nEssence of Xandivious Xandivious' Demon Bag\nReach 42000 reputation with Timbermaw Hold\nProvided: Demon Summoning Torch","desc":"‹name›, thanks to you we have devised a way to summon forth the root of all evil for the Winterfall tribe - the corrupting demon that dominates them!\nTake this torch to the mouth of High Chief Winterfall's personal cave and plant it there. Doing so will force the demon to reveal itself and investigate. This is when you and your allies must strike it down! Only the essence of the fallen demon will begin the lengthy healing process of the Winterfall tribe... and the salvation of Timbermaw Hold.","rew":"You will receive:\nDefender of the Timbermaw\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Timbermaw Hold","back":"You have returned to us, ‹name›... does this mean that the demon has been slain?","done":"You've... you've saved us! Your defeat of the demon Xandivious has ensured the safety of Timbermaw Hold for years to come. You are truly a hero amongst our kind.\nPlease, accept this with our blessing. Though the healing process will be slow amongst the furbolgs - and the conflict will still go on - you have given the Winterfall something they never had before this day.\nThey have a chance at survival.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":65.2,"y":2.7,"n":"Gorn One Eye","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"3121":{"id":3121,"t":"A Strange Request","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Shrunken Head to Neeru Fireblade in Orgrimmar.\nA Shrunken Head\nProvided: A Shrunken Head","desc":"Neeru Fireblade in Orgrimmar has what I need to get started here! He has mixed up a concoction that I need for my... well, you'll see.\nOff with you now -- to Orgrimmar. Here, take this with you. It's a shrunken head that I promised Neeru in exchange for the herbs. It's the head of some poor dwarf I ventured across in the forest. I'm sure Neeru will be pleased.\nYou'll find Neeru in the Cleft of Shadow.","rew":"Experience: 1,950\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Yes?","done":"I have been waiting for Uzer'i to deliver this...\nLet me give you the herb mixture I prepared for his... well, experiments...\nFeralas Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.4,"y":43.4,"n":"Witch Doctor Uzer'i","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":49.5,"y":50.6,"n":"Neeru Fireblade","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"3841":{"id":3841,"t":"An Orphan Looking For a Home","lv":47,"min":38,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Quentin in Thousand Needles.\nUnhatched Sprite Darter Egg\nProvided: Unhatched Sprite Darter Egg","desc":"Oh, hello, ‹name›. I'm so glad to see you again. How was your trip to Darnassus?\nWell, you'll be happy to know that we've made quite a bit of progress while you've been gone. We even saved a nest full of eggs. Unfortunately, the mother died before we got to her.\nSay, would you want one for a pet? They look to hatch soon, so they'll need a good father/mother. What do you say?\nIf you're really interested, take one of the eggs to Quentin at the race tracks in Shimmering Flats. He'll tell you more.","rew":"Experience: 1,050\n+25 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Why hello, ‹class›.\nDon't let my location fool you, I'm really not here for the races... as entertaining as they may be.\nI'm actually here in Thousand Needles investigating all I can to find out how salvageable the land is. It has become my crusade of sorts to revitalize and replenish the area with new, fertile soil. Perhaps I'll find there's a water source nearby.\nTell me you haven't noticed how odd the transition between Feralas and Thousand Needles is. Strange magic was afoot when that happened.","done":"Ah, a sprite darter egg, and one near maturation, if I'm not mistaken. Remarkable you've found one, let alone in this good a condition. They're rarely seen in Feralas these days. I understand there were various poachers in the area trying to capture and kill them for many reasons. Too bad really... such beautiful creatures when they reach adulthood.\nHow did you come across such a find?\nFeralas Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":65.9,"y":45.7,"n":"Kindal Moonweaver","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":78.3,"y":74.7,"n":"Quentin","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"561":{"id":561,"t":"Farren's Proof","lv":32,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Lieutenant Farren Orinelle in Southshore.","desc":"Please inform Lieutenant Orinelle that I would like him to refocus his efforts on the naga infesting the Eastern Strand. When he has results, tell him to report to me in person.","rew":"Experience: 260","done":"The naga, eh? Redpath must have just received the same information as me... Ha! He'll not receive a promotion from my toil. Let me explain.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":49.5,"y":58.7,"n":"Marshal Redpath","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":51.5,"y":58.4,"n":"Lieutenant Farren Orinelle","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"6721":{"id":6721,"t":"The Hunter's Path","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Dazalar in Dolanaar.","desc":"Hello, young hunter. You look to me like you are skilled enough to handle a beast and train it as your companion.\nYou must see Dazalar in Dolanaar. He can put you on the path to earning a pet of your own.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Yes, it is time, ‹class›.\nDun Morogh Teldrassil","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":34.4,"n":"Regnus Thundergranite","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.7,"y":59.5,"n":"Dazalar","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"6081":{"id":6081,"t":"Training the Beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Ormak Grimshot in Orgrimmar.","desc":"You now have the power to tame a pet, but you must also gain the skills to train it.\nTravel to Orgrimmar. There you must speak to one of our most revered hunters, Ormak Grimshot. He will give you the ability to train your new pet. You will find him in the Valley of Honor.\nGood luck, ‹name›.","rew":"You will learn: Training Lesson\nExperience: 420","done":"A young ‹class›, I see. Yes, I will grant you the skills you need to train and guide your pet. Not only will you be able to teach your pet new abilities, you will now be able to feed your pet, as well as revive it, should it fall in battle.\nNow, go, ‹class›. We will speak again, at a later date.\nDurotar Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":51.8,"y":43.5,"n":"Thotar","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":66,"y":18.5,"n":"Ormak Grimshot","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"3201":{"id":3201,"t":"At Last!","lv":48,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Proof of Deed back to Mountaineer Pebblebitty.\nProof of Deed\nProvided: Proof of Deed","desc":"I can't believe Pebblebitty doubted the authenticity of the horn. Between you and me, I think she's just jealous. I know she really wanted to kill that beast herself, what with the 'incident' and all.\nSo you need a proof of deed? After the contribution you just made to the museum, it won't be a problem.\n<Curator Thorius begins to fill out a large document.>\nThere we go! You can take that back to Pebblebitty.","rew":"You will receive:\nKey to Searing Gorge\nExperience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"I don't believe it.","done":"I don't know how someone as weak as you overcame Margol, but a deal is a deal. Here is the key.\nIf anything happens to you after this, it will be your own fault.\nDun Morogh Loch Modan","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.6,"y":23.6,"n":"Curator Thorius","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":18.2,"y":84,"n":"Mountaineer Pebblebitty","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"161":{"id":161,"t":"A Dark Threat Looms","lv":18,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Chief Engineer Hinderweir wants you to take the strange smelling powder to Ashlan Stonesmirk, the explosives expert in Dun Modr.\nStrange Smelling Powder\nProvided: Strange Smelling Powder","desc":"If my suspicions are correct, this is some type of explosive powder. This must be analyzed by an explosives expert so we know just what we're dealing with here. Ashlan Stonesmirk was assigned to the regiment guarding Dun Modr and the Thandol Span. I need you to make a grave and perilous journey, ‹name›.\nTravel through the Algaz Gate, follow the road through the Wetlands and seek out Stonesmirk in Dun Modr. Heed my advice: stick to the roads and stop for nothing!","rew":"Experience: 1,350\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"You say somethin', sonny? Can't hear a bloody thing besides the ringin' in me ears. Say, what's that you got there?","done":"Ah, well Ol' Hinderweir is wise to be worried.\nLoch Modan Wetlands","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":46,"y":13.6,"n":"Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":50,"y":18.2,"n":"Ashlan Stonesmirk","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"8881":{"id":8881,"t":"Large Cluster Rockets","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Coin of Ancestry","rew":"You will receive:\nLarge Cluster Rocket Recipes Lunar Festival Fireworks Pack","back":"Large cluster rockets require vast resources and skill to create, but their brilliance and beauty is worth that effort! Bring me coins of ancestry and I will grant you the knowledge of their crafting.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Here is the recipe for large cluster rockets. May your products bring joy and luck to all those who gaze up them.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":53.8,"y":35.3,"n":"Fariel Starsong","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8721":{"id":8721,"t":"Starweave the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"The heavens, in their countless stars, hold answers to earthly mysteries, ‹name›. Might, then, the wise, and the lucky, gaze up and find truth?","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":36.8,"y":46.8,"n":"Elder Starweave","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"92481":{"id":92481,"t":"A student of the arcane","lv":2,"min":2,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Examine the Glowing Recall Crystal, then speak with Dorii Brightwhisper in Thendal Grove.\nProvided: Glowing Recall Crystal","desc":"While you were away dealing with our vuldren problem, our resident mage trainer--Dorii Brightwhisper--left this recall crystal for you. It contains some sort of message for you, so give it a look. Afterwards, you can find Dorii in the structure just behind me.","back":"Greetings, ‹name›. I'm pleased to have the privilege of furthering your magical studies.","done":"Let me have a look at you. Yes, I believe you will make a fine young ‹class›. The power of the arcane has waned amongst our people, but there are those who would seek to rediscover much of what we've lost in the millennia we've spent here amongst the clouds. I am sure that you will lead the charge in this never ending search for arcane knowledge, and ultimately make us proud.\nSpeak with me again if you wish to take your next steps.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42,"y":23.4,"n":"Rorian the Dayseeker","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":41.6,"y":23.6,"n":"Dorii Brightwhisper","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"1921":{"id":1921,"t":"Gathering Materials","lv":15,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Linen Cloth and the 6 Charged Rift Gems to Wynne Larson in Stormwind.\n10 Linen Cloth Kogan Forgestone , Lisan Pierce , Adam Lind 66.7 % , Hidden Strongbox 58.6 % and 4 more\n6 Charged Rift Gem Miners' League Crates","desc":"You have served your fellow mages well, and now it is time to don your wizard's robe. Wynne Larson can make your robe, but you must bring her the needed materials\nThe robe will be made of linen which is easy to find, but you must also gain charged rift gems, and the only known location of the gems is in the Silver Stream Mine of Loch Modan, left in crates by the dwarven miners' league.\nGather the linen and the gems and bring them to Wynne Larson at the Larson Clothiers in the Mage District.","rew":"Experience: 800","back":"Hello, ‹name›. Jennea told me you would come. Do you have something for me?","done":"Yes, these are great pieces of linen. I can make a fine robe with them. And after I weave the rift gems into it, we'll have a garment fit for a mage!\nStormwind City Loch Modan","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.6,"y":85.8,"n":"Jennea Cannon","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":51.8,"y":83.5,"n":"Wynne Larson","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"7041":{"id":7041,"t":"Vyletongue Corruption","lv":47,"min":41,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Fill the Coated Cerulean Vial at the orange crystal pool in Maraudon.\nUse the Filled Cerulean Vial on the Vylestem Vines to force the corrupted Noxxious Scion to emerge.\nHeal 8 plants by killing these Noxxious Scion, then return to Talendria in Nijel's Point.\nFilled Cerulean Vial\nVylestem Vines healed : 0/ 8\nProvided: Coated Cerulean Vial","desc":"A satyr known as Vyletongue has corrupted the caverns of Maraudon, stunting the growth of many of the plants inside.\nTake this vial, ‹name›. Fill it at the corrupted orange pool found inside the caverns; the coating inside the vial will counter the toxins, turning it into a healing agent.\nFind the Vylestem vines inside the orange caverns, and use the purified liquid on them. The corruption will be purged from the plant, but do know that Vyletongue will still control it. He may use it against you...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWoodseed Hoop Sagebrush Girdle Branchclaw Gauntlets\nExperience: 5,250","back":"If you are able to heal the plant, it will again begin to grow. We must do what we can, ‹name›...","done":"Thank you for returning this, ‹name›. With the remaining liquid you brought me, I can continue my studies.\nWhile there is still much to do, you have helped to heal some of the corruption that Vyletongue spread through Maraudon. Please take this with my gratitude.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":68.5,"y":8.9,"n":"Talendria","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["maraudon"]},"96241":{"id":96241,"t":"Talkin bout toxins mon","lv":30,"min":23,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Use the Toxin Extractor to gather 5 Gloomrise Toxin Samples from the Gnawed Corpses at Gloomrise.\n5 Gloomrise Toxin Sample\nProvided: Toxin Extractor","desc":"Something funny be happenin' over there at Gloomrise. Ol' Mazu'kon be hearin all about these nasty new beasties skitterin' all around there.\nSome say those creepy crawlies got a venom that have some unique properties and this be gettin' me curious. Take my extractor. Use it on the dead bodies layin' around that place to harvest the venom. Do this and I be in ya debt, mon.","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,450\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls\n+100 reputation with Earthen Ring","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":32.4,"y":20.6,"n":"Mazu'kon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9041":{"id":9041,"t":"Dreadnaught Waistguard","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Korfax at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Dreadnaught Waistguard if you bring him the following items: 1 Desecrated Waistguard, 8 Wartorn Plate Scraps, 1 Arcanite Bar and 5 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Waistguard Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Heigan the Unclean 0 % in Naxxramas , Noth the Plaguebringer 0 % in Naxxramas\n8 Wartorn Plate Scrap Infectious Ghoul 22.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 21.6 % in Naxxramas , Plagued Deathhound 21.3 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 20.8 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\nArcanite Bar\n5 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"During your battles with the Scourge in Naxxramas, should you come across desecrated battlements and wartorn plate scraps, return them to me and I shall craft for you a piece of armor worn by heroes.","rew":"You will receive:\nDreadnaught Waistguard\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Dreadnaught Waistguard.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":72,"y":48.5,"n":"Korfax, Champion of the Light","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"81":{"id":81,"t":"Ripple Delivery","lv":48,"min":42,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the barrel to Dran Droffers in Orgrimmar.\nDran's Ripple Delivery\nProvided: Dran's Ripple Delivery","desc":"I have taken the extra step of securing not only Dran's packaged ripple in the barrel, but also the extra bottles of ripple he is purloining. While I may not hold Dran very highly, there is nothing worse than jostled ripple. You're welcome.\nNow, deliver yon barrel to Dran Droffers in his salvage emporium in Orgrimmar. Pray tell, please extend my warmest greetings to Malton; let him know that should he ever thirst for fine drink and finer drinking companions, we would be honored with his visit.","rew":"Money: 1 40 1 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"If you're not here to buy anything, and you're not here to deliver anything, then you're wasting my time! You better have that ripple!","done":"Well, let's see what's in this barrel!\nYes, yes, it looks as though it is all here. Here's your fee for the package, good job on that. I stand to make five times that fee when I sell it to the tavern! Har har!\nThese extra bottles of Hinterlands Honey Ripple are going to be set for a special occasion. I think I'll drink some with champagne. I'll call it... champipple.\nThe Hinterlands Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":26.7,"y":48.6,"n":"Gilveradin Sunchaser","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":59.6,"y":36.5,"n":"Dran Droffers","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"3681":{"id":3681,"t":"Tome of Divinity","lv":12,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.","desc":"Sorry to interrupt your travels, ‹race›, but I thought you should know that word was sent from Stormwind recently asking that paladins report there for training.\nIf I didn't know any better, I'd say your close to reaching a special time and it's time you started studying the Tomes.\nLook for Duthorian Rall in Stormwind. He usually trains paladins in the Cathedral of Light.","rew":"Experience: 230","done":"Welcome to the Cathedral of Light, ‹class›.\nDun Morogh Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":54.8,"y":22.1,"n":"Brandur Ironhammer","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.5,"y":47.5,"n":"Duthorian Rall","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5761":{"id":5761,"t":"Slaying the Beast","lv":16,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,350 experience instead of 1,150, 2.04 times as much. Read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Enter Ragefire Chasm and slay Taragaman the Hungerer, then bring his heart back to Neeru Fireblade in Orgrimmar.\nTaragaman the Hungerer's Heart Taragaman the Hungerer","desc":"The primary task set upon me by our great Warchief is to root out the creatures responsible for infesting our lord's great city with demonic influence. The Burning Blade is one threat, but there are others; the Searing Blade for instance, who make their home in Ragefire Chasm, secretly attempting to subvert innocent members of the Horde.\nIf they are to be stopped, then their leader must be slain--a Felguard named Taragaman the Hungerer.\nKill him, and his heart will appease Thrall, of this I'm sure.","rew":"Money: 8 0 gold, 8 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,350","back":"Have you killed the beast? He surely must be the leader of the Searing Blade in Ragefire Chasm.","done":"Ha! You've done it! Thrall will be so pleased.\nI will ensure this heart is taken care of properly.\nFor now though, you must celebrate your victory. I will inform Thrall of your success.\nThank you for your aid, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":49.5,"y":50.6,"n":"Neeru Fireblade","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ragefire-chasm"]},"2241":{"id":2241,"t":"The Apple Falls","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 420 experience instead of 400, 1.05 times as much.","obj":"Take Jannok's Rose to Syurna in Darnassus.\nJannok's Rose\nProvided: Jannok's Rose","desc":"They say I'm 'lovestruck,' whatever that means.\nSure, I spend my every waking moment thinking about Syurna. Sure, my home is full of paintings and drawings of Syurna. Sure, I often go days without eating, sleeping, or drinking, while I lament about the love we could have had. Is that so wrong?\nNow she won't see me! ME! I've tried sending her messages but she won't even talk to another person unless they are a rogue.\nCould you deliver this flower to her? Don't forget to tell her it's from Jannok.","rew":"Experience: 420","back":"Oh, isn't this wonderful. You've brought flowers for your own funeral.","done":"Had I saved every flower that dolt, Jannok, had sent me, I would have had the means to open a shop. Regardless, it seems as if Jannok's latest courier may prove to be useful.Interested in some work, ‹class›?\nTeldrassil Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.4,"y":60.1,"n":"Jannok Breezesong","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":37,"y":21.9,"n":"Syurna","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"3441":{"id":3441,"t":"Divine Retribution","lv":48,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Listen as Kalaran Windblade tells his story.","desc":"Hear my tale, adventurer.","rew":"Experience: 440","back":"Allow me to finish mo... ‹race›.","done":"Have you heard enough? Are you prepared to act?","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":39.1,"y":39,"n":"Kalaran Windblade","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"8241":{"id":8241,"t":"Restoring Fiery Flux Supplies via Iron","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Incendosaur Scale Incendosaur\n4 Iron Bar\nCoal Dalaran Miner , Blazing Elemental 28.4 % , Inferno Elemental 24.7 % , Molten Giant 24.7 % and 4 more","desc":"Let's not waste more of my precious time with jibber jabber, ‹race›. It's time to focus on replenishing our dwindling fiery flux supply.\nWhat I'm gonna need from you is the following:\n*Incendosaur scales.\n*Iron bars.\n*Coal.\nI'll take all that you can offer!\nAnd you'll do it fast if you wanna get in good with the Brotherhood.","back":"Let's not waste more of my precious time with jibber jabber, ‹race›. It's time to focus on replenishing our dwindling fiery flux supply.\nWhat I'm gonna need from you is the following:\n*Incendosaur scales.\n*Iron bars.\n*Coal.\nI'll take all that you can offer!\nAnd you'll do it fast if you wanna get in good with the Brotherhood.","done":"There's always room for more fiery flux, junior. Keep it comin'... unless I tell you to stop.","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":38.8,"y":28.5,"n":"Master Smith Burninate","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"6961":{"id":6961,"t":"Great-father Winter is Here!","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Greatfather Winter; he is located near the Smokywood Pastures vendor area in Orgrimmar.","desc":"Have a wondrous Winter Veil, friend! Be sure to say hello to Greatfather Winter! If you've been nice this year, you'll receive wondrous treats on the day of the Feast of Winter Veil. Be sure to tell him what you hope to get this year!\nAlso, be sure to stock up on treats to give those who've been nice this year. We have a great selection to choose from. Fresh from our farm to your plate - it's Smokywood Pastures wholesome goodness!","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"Ho ho hello. I am Greatfather Winter, and I - courtesy of the fine folks of Smokywood Pastures... \"Fresh from our farm to your plate, it's Smokywood Pastures wholesome goodness\" - would like to wish you a fantastic Feast of Winter Veil.\nIf you've been good this year, maybe you will receive treats from Smokywood Pastures as your treat for the Feast of Winter Veil. Huzzah.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":53.3,"y":66.5,"n":"Kaymard Copperpinch","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":52.5,"y":69.2,"n":"Great-father Winter","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"1521":{"id":1521,"t":"Call of Earth","lv":4,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Rough Quartz to Seer Ravenfeather in Camp Narache.\nRough Quartz\nProvided: Rough Quartz","desc":"Take this rough quartz from me and bring it to Seer Ravenfeather as proof of our meeting. She will craft a totem for you, and this pebble will be the heart of it. As small as it may seem, you will come to find that size does not matter, and that even the smallest of things can outlast mountains.\nBe patient, ‹name›. Remain strong. And seek wisdom. This is what earth asks of you. In the end, you shall become one with the earth--respect it as it shall respect you.","rew":"You will receive:\nEarth Totem\nYou will learn: Stoneskin Totem\nExperience: 450","back":"Greetings, ‹name›. You would not return to me if you had not accomplished your task. May I be the first to welcome you fully to the first path of four that will forever rule your travels.\nIf you have the stone the earth gave to you, I will give you the totem it promised. If not, then I pity you. There is much pride to be had when you've fully dedicated yourself to the elements.","done":"Splendid.\nThe totem I will craft for you is more than a symbol--it has abilities beyond that. One use of the totem is a focus for spells. Those spells are tied to the earth, and as you earn greater and greater wisdom, more of the earth's abilities will be made accessible to you. Trainers found throughout Kalimdor will know when you are ready for greater knowledge and will let you know as much when you visit them.\nBut for now, take this earth totem, and a scroll to teach you your first ability.\nDurotar Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":44,"y":76.2,"n":"Minor Manifestation of Earth","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":52,"y":80.4,"n":"Minor Manifestation of Earth","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":44.3,"y":76.8,"n":"Seer Ravenfeather","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"93041":{"id":93041,"t":"Facing the truth","lv":38,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis Clan, and bring an Accursed Skull and Gelkis Necromantic Garb to Uthek the Wise in Gelkis Village.\nAccursed Skull\nGelkis Clan Centaur\nProvided: Gelkis Necromantic Garb","desc":"This discovery is devastating for our clan, but it is in our best interest to keep this only to those who need to know. Uthek is one such person who needs to be aware of what is going on here. I suspect she will know how to proceed.\nTake this to show her. For good measure, we should also bring evidence of the necromancy itself to her. Find a skull that looks recently cursed. I suspect they may be hoarding them in the maws of one of the goliath's skeletons.\nLevel 38 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 36 41 48 Side Both factions Quest ID 93041\nThe chain\n10 quests from level 32 to 38, 14,740 XP in all.\n1 [ 35 ] Strange Alliance\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Gelkis, then speak with Uthek the Wise.\nCaptain Pentigast Desolace\n2,050 XP\n2 [ 32 ] Raid on the Kolkar\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring 10 Crude Charms to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village in Desolace.\nUthek the Wise Desolace\n2,550 XP\n[ 33 ] Gelkis Alliance\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Gelkis, then speak with Uthek the Wise.\nGurda Wildmane Desolace\n650 XP\n3 [ 35 ] Stealing Supplies\nBring 6 bags of Crudely Dried Meat to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village.\nUthek the Wise Desolace\n1,350 XP\n4 [ 37 ] Ongeku\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring a Draenethyst Shard to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village in Desolace.\nUthek the Wise Desolace\n2,850 XP\n5 [ 38 ] Valley of Bones\nImprove your reputation with the Gelkis, and locate Nerlokh near the Valley of Bones far east of Gelkis Village.\n290 XP\n6 [ 38 ] Ravaging Ravagers\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis Clan and slay 6 Undead Ravagers, then return to Nerlokh at the southern entrance to Valley of Bones.\n1,450 XP\n7 [ 38 ] Facing the Truth this quest\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis Clan, and bring an Accursed Skull and Gelkis Necromantic Garb to Uthek the Wise in Gelkis Village.\n700 XP\n8 [ 38 ] A Cleansing Cry\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring Tears of Theradras back to Uthek the Wise in Gelkis Village.\n2,150 XP\n9 [ 38 ] Test Your Theory\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and dispel the necromantic curse present on the Accursed Skull.\n700 XP","cats":["shendralas"]},"8321":{"id":8321,"t":"Vyral the Vile","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Vyral's Signet Ring to Huum Wildmane in Cenarion Hold.\nVyral's Signet Ring Vyral the Vile","desc":"We have discovered another base of operations for the Twilight's Hammer. It is called Twilight's Run; it is a cave tucked in the northeast corner of Silithus. The local leader of the cult, Vyral the Vile, haunts that cave - it is he who you must next defeat. When you have done this, bring me his signet ring.\nFortune to you, ‹name›. The horrors of Twilight's Run are formidable indeed.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDesert Wind Gauntlets Sunprism Pendant\nMoney: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"‹name›, have you yet defeated Vyral the Vile? Do you have his signet ring?","done":"You've done it! Vyral is killed! This can only mean doom for the Twilight Hammer's operations in Silithus. There may be more of them scurrying about, but the blow you dealt to the cult today is one from which they will not easily recover.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":48.6,"y":37.9,"n":"Huum Wildmane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"6321":{"id":6321,"t":"Supplying the Sepulcher","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Podrig's Order to Karos Razok.\nPodrig's Order\nProvided: Podrig's Order","desc":"Executor Hadrec asked me to take stock of our equipment at the Sepulcher. With the Scourge, and worse, lurking in the woods, he doesn't want the Deathguards to lack gear they might need.\nI found that we are, in general, well stocked, but we do need more weapons to replace those lost in the field.\nHere is a requisition order of what is needed, for the weapon dealer Gordon Wendham in the Undercity. Take the order to our bat master, Karos Razok, and speak with him about transport to the Undercity.","rew":"Experience: 210\n+25 reputation with Undercity","back":"You appear to be on official business...","done":"Ah, an order for supplies. You will want to take this to the Undercity, no doubt. And quickly, for the Sepulcher must not be left under stocked.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":43.4,"y":41.7,"n":"Deathguard Podrig","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":45.6,"y":42.6,"n":"Karos Razok","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"91921":{"id":91921,"t":"Return to quinn again","lv":11,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring Quinn's potion to Quinn Yorick at the Ivar Patch, north of the Sepulcher.\nProvided: Quinn's Potion","desc":"Here is the new potion to aid in Quinn's recovery, made with love extracted from six whole hearts.\nNow, please excuse me before your presence necessitates more paperwork.","back":"You return! I was beginning to come to terms with devolving into a ghoul.","done":"<Quinn takes the potion and drinks it.>\nYes, I can feel it working. I will soon be able to travel.\nYou have done me a great favor, Saixgone.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":42.8,"y":40.8,"n":"Apothecary Renferrel","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":53.4,"y":12.6,"n":"Quinn Yorick","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"481":{"id":481,"t":"Dalar's Analysis","lv":14,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the rune-inscribed pendant to Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher.\nRune-inscribed Pendant\nProvided: Rune-inscribed Pendant","desc":"Take the pendant to Dalar Dawnweaver, perhaps he can shed some light on the wizards' plans.","rew":"Experience: 100\n+10 reputation with Undercity","back":"Yes, ‹class›? What is it?","done":"Interesting, more machinations of the Kirin Tor, it would seem. This is a powerful artifact. It was used frequently by powerful wizards of the Kirin Tor to channel magical energies.\nThat they are delivering so many to Ambermill indicates that they must be undergoing a project of some magnitude.\nI will see if I can pierce their shields and ascertain their intent.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":44,"y":40.9,"n":"Shadow Priest Allister","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":44.2,"y":39.8,"n":"Dalar Dawnweaver","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"84401":{"id":84401,"t":"Scourge undead menace or misunderstood","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Scourge: Undead Menace or Misunderstood?","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper Experience: 650","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nScourge: Undead Menace or Misunderstood? (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":38.6,"y":79.4,"n":"Jennea Cannon","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.4,"y":32.4,"n":"Oran Snakewrithe","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"6401":{"id":6401,"t":"Kaya's Alive","lv":18,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Tell Tammra Windfield in Sun Rock Retreat the good news.","desc":"Tell Tammra Windfield, Kaya's aunt who's at Sun Rock Retreat, about the good news! Kaya is alive! We had thought she was lost after the brutal attack on our village. Follow the path to the west to get to Sun Rock Retreat.","rew":"Money: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,000\n+75 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"My goodness, my niece Kaya is alive! That is good news indeed. Thank you, ‹name›.\nThe Barrens Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":35.2,"y":27.8,"n":"Makaba Flathoof","s":1},{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":47.5,"y":58.4,"n":"Tammra Windfield","e":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"6481":{"id":6481,"t":"Earthen Arise","lv":20,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Raptorcrest Bracers.","obj":"Open the Resonite cask with the Enchanted Resonite Crystal, and then slay Goggeroc. Return to Mor'rogal with the news and Enchanted Resonite Crystal.\nEnchanted Resonite Crystal\nGoggeroc slain\nProvided: Enchanted Resonite Crystal","desc":"You have uncovered a dark threat to the land, ‹class›. The Resonite cask you have found in that cave houses a slumbering Earthen by the name of Goggeroc.\nI have changed the mixture of the Resonite crystals that you gathered with my shamanistic powers. Take the enchanted Resonite crystal and smash open the Resonite cask, which houses the Earthen.\nWhen awakened, Goggeroc will be weakened... Slay him, ‹name›!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nOwlbeard Bracers Wolfmane Wristguards Raptorcrest Bracers\nNew in Forever: Raptorcrest Bracers.\nExperience: 1,550\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"I fear if we do not dispose of this threat immediately, all of Stonetalon will be lost. The might of an Earthen can not be matched by any means. When awakened, Goggeroc will be weak from his long slumber, this will be the opportunity that you must take advantage of... go now ‹name›!","done":"You bear good news, ‹class›! I fear the possibilities of what an Earthen would mean to Kalimdor.\nSlaying Goggeroc was a task for no one less then a hero. You have done well; all of Stonetalon and Kalimdor are indebted to you, noble ‹class›.\nAccept this as your reward most honored one.\nStonetalon Mountains Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":47.2,"y":64,"n":"Mor'rogal","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"80001":{"id":80001,"t":"Rekindle","lv":40,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Simple Wood\nFlint and Tinder","rew":"You will receive:\nFlint and Tinder","back":"An extinguished fire pit. The wood is even dry enough to catch a flame.\nSimple Wood (1)\nFlint and Tinder (1)","done":"You put your scout skills to work.","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":40.6,"y":52.4,"n":"Firepit","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"2641":{"id":2641,"t":"Sprinkle's Secret Ingredient","lv":49,"min":44,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Sprinkle in Gadgetzan wants you to collect a Violet Tragan and return it to her.\nViolet Tragan Violet Tragan","desc":"When I was a kid, my sister used to do all the cooking. It was horrible! I could barely stomach some of her concoctions -- until I found what I like to call my \"secret\" ingredient! Add it to anything, and... WOW! It tastes great!\nWhat is it, you ask? It's a mushroom called the Violet Tragan. If you want me to help you turn this horrid-tasting brew into something edible, head to the Hinterlands, and look for a small lake there.\nOh, and remember, the Violet Tragan can only be found underwater.","rew":"Experience: 4,550\n+100 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"Under the waters of that lake -- it's the only place where the Violet Tragan can be found. Hope you're good at holding your breath!","done":"That's the stuff, ‹name›!\nIt looks so good, I might just... Haha, gotcha!\nTanaris The Hinterlands","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.1,"y":26.9,"n":"Sprinkle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"3521":{"id":3521,"t":"Iverron's Antidote","lv":4,"min":2,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 7 Hyacinth Mushrooms, 4 Moonpetal Lilies, and 1 Webwood Ichor for Dirania Silveshine in Shadowglen.\n7 Hyacinth Mushroom Hyacinth Mushroom , Grellkin 80 %\n4 Moonpetal Lily Moonpetal Lily\nWebwood Ichor Webwood Spider 80 %","desc":"We may be able to help Iverron, as I know of an antidote that should help with the poison. It requires some ingredients, though, before I can make it.\nI'll need Hyacinth mushrooms. You can find these growing under trees, or you may collect them from the grell south of here; they seem to have taken a liking to them. I'll also need Moonpetal lilies, which only grow around watery pools.\nThe last ingredient may prove the most difficult. From the very spiders that poisoned Iverron, collect Webwood ichor.","rew":"Experience: 360\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Please, collect the ingredients, ‹name›. Iverron needs our help.","done":"Thank Elune that you have gathered these ingredients so quickly!\nIn just a moment, I will have the antidote prepared.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":60.9,"y":42,"n":"Dirania Silvershine","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"2561":{"id":2561,"t":"Druid of the Claw","lv":10,"min":3,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Oben Rageclaw wants you to kill his soulless body, and then use the Voodoo Charm.\nRageclaw slain\nProvided: Voodoo Charm","desc":"After examining this charm, ‹name›, I see now what must be done. Please take it, and do as I ask.\nYou are to explore the deepest areas of the Ban'ethil Barrow Den. There, you will find my soulless body... Although I regret what I am about to tell you, I see no other way to free myself from the control of the Gnarlpine.\nIn order for me to escape them, you must kill my physical form. Once that is done, use the voodoo charm on my fallen body. After you have completed this task, please return to me.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSleeping Robes Brushwood Blade\nExperience: 1,050\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"‹name›, be wary when approaching my physical form; the enchantment it is under is quite powerful.","done":"I am finally free of the control of the Gnarlpine. Thank you, ‹name›.\nMy spirit may now rest peacefully forever in the Emerald Dream.\nPerhaps one day we may meet again, young ‹class›. But, for now, please accept this reward as a symbol of my gratitude.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":44.9,"y":61.6,"n":"Oben Rageclaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"5041":{"id":5041,"t":"Supplies for the Crossroads","lv":14,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find and return Crossroads' Supply Crates to Thork in the Barrens.\nCrossroads' Supply Crates Crossroads' Supply Crates","desc":"That attack on the caravan contained supplies we desperately needed.\nYou've been brave enough to take on the Razormane tribe so far, and I will ask you to do so again, but this time, I wonder if I could ask you to keep your eyes open for some of our lost supplies. You can probably find them throughout their camps, the quilboar getting fat off their dishonorable acts.\nThe people of the Crossroads would be in your debt.","rew":"Money: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 975\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"How goes your search for the supplies, ‹name›? I trust the quilboar fall under your strength easily.","done":"Haha! Thank you, ‹name›! This will help us greatly. You're a boon to the Crossroads and to the Horde. If there is anything I can do for you, please, let me know.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.5,"y":30.9,"n":"Thork","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"3921":{"id":3921,"t":"Wenikee Boltbucket","lv":14,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Broken Samophlange to Wenikee Boltbucket.\nBroken Samophlange\nProvided: Broken Samophlange","desc":"I think I might have broken that Samophlange. That's not good, because I already told some colleagues in Undermine about it and they were very intrigued. We must find a way to fix it!\nTake the broken samophlange to Wenikee Boltbucket, just south of Mor'shan Rampart, the horde outpost between the Barrens and Ashenvale. She is very clever and inquisitive. If you show her the samophlange I bet she'd jump at the chance to fix it.","rew":"Experience: 490\n+50 reputation with Ratchet\n+25 reputation with Horde","back":"I'm very busy with my work, ‹class›. Unless you have something for me, it'd be best if you moved along...","done":"Oh, what's this? A samophlange, you say? What's a samophlange??\nAh... but look at the way it moves when you handle it. And there's the sound of intricate gears inside. Oh my! I want to fix it and see what it does, don't you??","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":63,"y":37.2,"n":"Sputtervalve","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":49.1,"y":11.2,"n":"Wenikee Boltbucket","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"881":{"id":881,"t":"Echeyakee","lv":16,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Echeyakee's Hide to Sergra Darkthorn at the Crossroads.\nEcheyakee's Hide Echeyakee\nProvided: Horn of Echeyakee","desc":"Whitemist, Echeyakee in the Tauren tongue, is the king of the savannah cats. He hunts with such stealth, they say he's like a thin, white mist on the earth. And he kills so fast his prey have no time for fear, or pain.\nThe Tauren say he is both mercy and death.\nYou will learn if that's true, for I now set you on the path to hunt Echeyakee. His lair is northeast of the Crossroads, among the bones of giant Kodo\nGo. Blow this horn when you reach his lair. Blow the horn, and he will come.","rew":"Experience: 1,450\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"The great cat calls to you, ‹name›.","done":"You've beaten Echeyakee, and though his days of hunting are over... his spirit is with you. He will show you the strength found in subtlety, and the honor in mercy.\nYour path is still long, ‹class›. Let's hope you stride it well.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.2,"y":31,"n":"Sergra Darkthorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"3281":{"id":3281,"t":"Stolen Silver","lv":18,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Stolen Silver to Gazrog in the Crossroads.\nStolen Silver Stolen Silver","desc":"You may have killed the raptors, but the silver they stole must be recovered! I have reports that the raptors have a large grouping of nests south of Ratchet, known as the Raptor Grounds. It is likely that they brought our stolen silver there.\nGo to this raptor haven and search for the stolen silver. When you find it, return it to me.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRambling Boots Settler's Leggings\nMoney: 10 0 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,350\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Do you have the silver?","done":"Aha! So the raptors did hide the silver at their lair. It's hard to believe these beasts would have the desire for silver. Perhaps the stories of their intelligence are not as far from the mark as I thought!\nThank you, ‹name›. Take this as a reward for your service to us, and know that the guards of the crossroads owe their next month's pay to you.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.9,"y":30.3,"n":"Gazrog","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"2881":{"id":2881,"t":"Troll Necklace Bounty","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Troll Tribal Necklace Hitah'ya the Keeper 20 % , Morta'gya the Keeper 20 % , Mith'rethis the Enchanter 20 % , Qiaga the Keeper 20 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 390\n+25 reputation with Wildhammer Clan","back":"You've done it already, but we will continue to accept any troll tribal necklaces you find and are willing to turn in. By turning them in to me, you'll continue to improve your standing amongst the Wildhammers; if you're willing to fight for us, then we'll be willing to fight for you!\nI need five troll tribal necklaces for them to count, ‹name›.","done":"Another set of necklaces means that there are fewer trolls in the Hinterlands we have to worry about!\nYou've done it again, ‹name›.\nKeep up the good work!","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":14.8,"y":44.6,"n":"Fraggar Thundermantle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"7841":{"id":7841,"t":"Message to the Wildhammer","lv":48,"min":44,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Otho Moji'ko at Revantusk Village in the Hinterlands wants you to slaughter 15 Highvale Outrunners, 15 Highvale Scouts, 15 Highvale Marksman and 15 Highvale Rangers. Return to him when this task is complete.\nYou can find the Highvale high elves at the Quel'Danil Lodge in the northwestern region of the Hinterlands.\nHighvale Scout slain : 0/ 15\nHighvale Outrunner slain : 0/ 15\nHighvale Ranger slain : 0/ 15\nHighvale Marksman slain : 0/ 15","desc":"The Wildhammer be striking up deals with our enemies, forgin' new alliances. This time, they be workin' with the high elves, mon.\n<Otho spits.>\nWe be needin' to send those Wildhammer dwarves a message - a message in the blood of our enemies. Slaughter every Highvale high elf that you come across, leave their bodies as a warnin'.\nNever mess with trolls!","rew":"Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Revantusk Trolls","back":"You be too clean, mon. You gotta mix it up - get down and dirty with the enemy.","done":"It be lookin' like the Revantusk are forgin' new alliances as well, mon! You done good.","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":79.4,"y":79.1,"n":"Otho Moji'ko","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"4881":{"id":4881,"t":"Assassination Plot","lv":28,"min":23,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Warn Kanati Greycloud at Whitereach Post of the plot to kill him.","desc":"The Tauren, Kanati Greycloud is bold to set up a hunting camp in Thousand Needles. We must kill him to rid this hunting camp and all who may follow him. We will converge at the small post Southwest of the Great Lift.","rew":"Experience: 2,300\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"They come to kill me? I will show them how a Tauren fights!","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":21.3,"y":32.1,"n":"Kanati Greycloud","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"5361":{"id":5361,"t":"Family Tree","lv":35,"min":32,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Cliffwatcher Longhorn Report to Nataka Longhorn at Ghost Walker Post in Desolace.\nCliffwatcher Longhorn Report\nProvided: Cliffwatcher Longhorn Report","desc":"My brother Nataka is stationed at Ghost Walker Post over in Desolace. I'd like to ask you... could you give this report to him for me? A year has passed since the last time I wrote, there has been unusual centaur activity since then and he should be informed.\nJourney to Stonetalon Mountain north of the Crossroads, and then head west into Charred Vale. From there, head south into Desolace; there you will find a road going south to Ghost Walker Post.","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,050\n+75 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"What news have you, ‹class›! Ah - a message from my brother you say? Well then, hand over the report!","done":"I know not what connection you have with my brother but it would seem he has trust with you, ‹class›.\nI am Nataka Longhorn and would like to welcome you to Ghost Walker Post, we have many needs of a ‹class›! Talk with others, perhaps there is need of you here.\nThousand Needles Desolace","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":45.7,"y":50.7,"n":"Cliffwatcher Longhorn","s":1},{"z":"Desolace","x":55.4,"y":55.8,"n":"Nataka Longhorn","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1121":{"id":1121,"t":"Get the Goblins Drunk","lv":44,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Fool's Stout to the Goblin Pit Boss.\nFool's Stout\nProvided: Fool's Stout","desc":"We need to try the Fool's Stout on one of the pit crews. If you want to try it on the goblins, then here -- take the stout and give it to the goblin pit boss.\nAnd don't wait too long. This stout will go bad eventually.","rew":"Experience: 380","back":"What are you looking at?","done":"What do we have here? Booze, eh?\nWell, I don't mind if we have just a little...","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":77.8,"y":77.3,"n":"Kravel Koalbeard","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":79.9,"y":76.7,"n":"Goblin Pit Boss","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"3761":{"id":3761,"t":"Un'Goro Soil","lv":50,"min":47,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Un'Goro Soil samples to Ghede on the Elder Rise of Thunder Bluff.\n20 Un'Goro Soil Un'Goro Dirt Pile , Gorishi Hive Guard 58.8 % , Gorishi Worker 55.8 % , Gorishi Stinger 55.2 % and 4 more","desc":"The soil of Un'Goro Crater is reportedly enriched with potent magical qualities. The Cenarion Circle wants to study this soil in large quantities; go into the wilds of Un'Goro and acquire enough of it for our continued research.\nThe rich soil will stick out in piles from time to time, and some of the beasts might have usable samples on their being. Take them all outside to Ghede; just look for the piles of dirt and the tauren barking orders. He means well, just don't get him riled up though!","rew":"Money: 1 45 1 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,700\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"At ease, Private. If you're here to unload soil from Un'Goro - outstanding then! Otherwise, disappear.","done":"Oh that's right Private ‹name›, don't make any effort to help me unload this soil up on to the piles! If the Great Spirits had wanted it done they would have miracled it up there, now wouldn't they?!\nArch Druid Runetotem wants to speak with you again, but for his next task you find that a journeyman's understanding of Herbalism would be helpful. If you don't know it though, he'll still find a use for you.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":78.6,"y":28.6,"n":"Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":77.5,"y":22,"n":"Ghede","e":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"721":{"id":721,"t":"A Sign of Hope","lv":35,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Hammertoe Grez in Uldaman.","desc":"‹name›, can ye find him? Can you find Hammertoe in Uldaman?\nIf those dirty Shadowforge are holdin' him hostage to figure out what he knows about the titan excavations, then all of Ironforge could be in huge trouble.\nFor a long time now those Dark Irons have been lookin' for magics to make more powerful golems. Hammertoe was doin' the same, of course, but only to stop them.\nThey're probably keepin' him alive until they learn what he knows.Ye've got to hurry if you're gonna save him!","rew":"Experience: 2,750\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","done":"Yes? Ah'm sorry... <cough> Feel so weak. Can ye come closer, ‹class›?\nRyedol sent ye? Muradin be praised, that boy's not as slow in the head as I once thought. <cough>\nBadlands Loch Modan","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":53.4,"y":43.4,"n":"Prospector Ryedol","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":37.3,"y":85.8,"n":"Hammertoe Grez","e":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"4321":{"id":4321,"t":"Making Sense of It","lv":53,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with J.D. Collie in a moment.","desc":"The information you have given me about the pylons is very interesting...\nGive me a moment to do some calculations, ‹name›. Speak to me again in a moment and I should be able to give you the answer we have been looking for.","rew":"You will receive:\nCrystal Pylon User's Manual\nExperience: 525","done":"Alright, ‹name›. This is fascinating... I can only hope that my diagrams are correct! I compiled everything into this manual, which you can have.\nI believe I can answer any questions you have about the crystals now, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":41.9,"y":2.7,"n":"J.D. Collie","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"92401":{"id":92401,"t":"A Frightened Request","lv":22,"min":15,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Investigate the disappearance of Edward Heartweaver in the Ruins of Lordaeron.\nInvestigate the disappearance of Edward Heartweaver in the Ruins of Lordaeron.","desc":"It's my husband Edward...\nHe has not returned from his weekly journey to the graveyard in the Lordaeron ruins. Our son was lost when Arthas razed the city, and my dear Edward is still filled with guilt and sorrow that we never found his body. I've tried to warn him against searching those overrun ruins, but he refuses to give up. I try not worry, but it's been days.\nThere are things there I cannot contend with but if you are willing, I need to know the fate of my husband.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nEdward's Knife Tabitha's Cuffs\nExperience: 4,600\n+150 reputation with Undercity","done":"What I asked of you was not fair, nor would it have been unjust for you to simply walk away. Thank you stranger. I am unable to repay you in kind but I hope one of these is acceptable.\nI hope our paths cross again without such sorrow.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":44.4,"y":42.8,"n":"Tabitha Heartweaver","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"4561":{"id":4561,"t":"Testing for Impurities - Un'Goro Crater","lv":52,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Un'Goro Slime Sample Muculent Ooze , Primal Ooze , Glutinous Ooze","rew":"You will receive:\nUn'Goro Tested Sample","back":"You take a sample of slime from Un'Goro Crater and place some of it into the various tubes and beakers on the table. As things begin to boil and spurt, the slime changes colors. When the process slows down and the liquids calm, you see a small petri dish with your purified Un'Goro slime samples in it along with some other remnants.","done":"You pick up the petri dish with the slime sample in it. The only way to discern if the samples is pure enough is to open it and examine the contents yourself. Ideally you'll find a sample that fits Chemist Fuely's criteria.\nDun Morogh Undercity Searing Gorge","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.2,"y":24.9,"n":"Testing Equipment","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":47.7,"y":73.6,"n":"Testing Equipment","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"65601":{"id":65601,"t":"Love hurts","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Magar in Orgrimmar.","desc":"A sayaad male is known as an incubus. A creature of profound evil and singular mind.\nThe demon must be lured into our world with an item of enticement - an object that represents great love and devotion.\nIf you trust a blind man to lead you, ‹name›, then listen. East from the Cleft of Shadow, along the main drag of Orgrimmar, lives Magar. He longs for the return of his mate, Krilge.\nSeek him out. He'll ask you to search for something precious. That is the key which you must bring to Gan'rul.","done":"Who told you about Krilge? Have you come with any news? You better not be toying with me...","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":47.2,"y":46.6,"n":"Cazul","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":63.4,"y":50,"n":"Magar","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"4961":{"id":4961,"t":"Cleansing of the Orb of Orahil","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill the Demon of the Orb, then speak with Tabetha.\nDemon of the Orb slain","desc":"Ah, a summoner's orb--this is where the taint must be coming from. We must exorcise the demon within it if you're to use it. That I can do easily.\nYou're the one who has the hard job. You must kill the demon once I release it.\nAnd you'll have to be quick. If you take too long then he'll return to the orb and we'll have to start over!\nSo get yourself ready, ‹name›. Prepare your strongest spells and keep your potions handy, and go get a friend if you have one. Because this isn't going to be pretty.","rew":"You will receive:\nCleansed Infernal Orb\nExperience: 2,350","back":"You'll have to kill that demon to remove its presence permanently from the orb, ‹name›.","done":"Nicely done, ‹name›! You gave that demon a lesson he won't soon forget. You've shown great power and skill. Now I suppose it's time you return to Menara with your cleansed orb so you can put it to good use.\nGood luck, ‹class›. Perhaps our paths will cross again.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":46.1,"y":57.1,"n":"Tabetha","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"7601":{"id":7601,"t":"What Niby Commands","lv":50,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Impsy in Felwood.","desc":"If I am to teach you the secrets of summoning an infernal servant, you must destroy Kroshius and bring me the infernal core from his burning remains. This, however, is not as easy as it sounds. Kroshius has all but burned out completely. You must reignite his corpse and raise him from the rubble. To do this, however, you must gather some components from other demonic entities.\nMy imp, Impsy, shall set you on your way.","done":"Oh boy, here we go again.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":41.6,"y":45.1,"n":"Niby the Almighty","s":1},{"z":"Felwood","x":41.5,"y":45,"n":"Impsy","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1681":{"id":1681,"t":"Ironband's Compound","lv":11,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a load of Umbral Ore to Tormus Deepforge in Ironforge.\nUmbral Ore Ironband's Strongbox","desc":"My mentor, Sturgy Ironband, had a compound south of Helm's Bed Lake in eastern Dun Morogh. There he taught blacksmithing and he was the best.\nBut one day, one of his students brought him a load of strange ore. Master Ironband called it umbral ore and was eager to work with it, but soon after it arrived... a band of Dark Iron dwarves attacked his compound. They killed everyone!\nEnter Ironband's compound, ‹name›, and avenge my master's death. And bring me the load of umbral ore that caused it.","rew":"Experience: 650","back":"Have you entered Ironband's Compound? Did you find the umbral ore?","done":"You found it! Well done!\nI hope you killed a host of Dark Iron dwarves while searching. I fear that Ironband's compound won't be the last place we see them.\nBut thank you for the ore, ‹name›. I'm eager to work it and find its properties.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.9,"y":27.9,"n":"Tormus Deepforge","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1841":{"id":1841,"t":"Velora Nitely and the Brutal Legguards","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Velora Nitely in the Undercity.","desc":"It is said that, before her death, Velora Nitely was one of the finest armorsmiths in Lordaeron. Death, it seems, has not decreased her talents. Speak with Velora--she will make your brutal legguards.\nVelora plies her trade in the Undercity of Lordaeron, in the trade quarter.","rew":"Experience: 1,200","done":"You are here for leg armor? Great!\nUm... am I making the armor for you, or are you making it for me?\nThat was joke. Was it funny? I can't tell... I lost my sense of humor the same time I lost my sense of smell. Which was about the same time I stopped breathing.\nThe Barrens Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":57.2,"y":30.3,"n":"Thun'grim Firegaze","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":62.1,"y":39.1,"n":"Velora Nitely","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8401":{"id":8401,"t":"Fight for Warsong Gulch","lv":49,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Gulch Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The Silverwing Sentinels are at war with the Warsong Outriders due to the destruction the Orcs are causing to the forest. There are, however, more reasons to defend this particular forest than the preservationist philosophy the Silverwings espouse.\nThe forest forms a strategic barrier that makes Ashenvale defendable against a large-scale attack. Without it, Astranaar would last a day or two before being annexed to the Barrens. Do your part in fighting the Warsong Outriders! For the Alliance!","rew":"Money: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,550\n+100 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels","back":"You've come back with news from the front, ‹name›?","done":"Good work, ‹name›. Thanks to you, our natural defenses in Ashenvale will remain intact for another day.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"5521":{"id":5521,"t":"Chromatic Mantle of the Dawn","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 25 Argent Dawn Valor Tokens to Quartermaster Lightspark at Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands.\n25 Argent Dawn Valor Token\nReach 42000 reputation with Argent Dawn","desc":"Brother/Sister ‹name› - your deeds on behalf of the Argent Dawn are far too numerous to be recounted easily. As a fitting tribute, I'll part with one of our special Chromatic Mantles of the Dawn - a version that protects the wearer from all forms of resistible magic simultaneously. Chromatic Mantles of the Dawn are reserved for only the mightiest of the Dawn's heroes!\nBring to me twenty-five valor tokens as a sign of tribute, and I'll give you the finest of all our mantles.","rew":"You will receive:\nChromatic Mantle of the Dawn\nExperience: 8,300\n+150 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Salutations, mighty ‹class›! Have you brought the valor tokens I asked of you? Once you hand them to me, I will issue you your own Chromatic Mantle of the Dawn.","done":"Most impressive, ‹name› - the Chromatic Mantle of the Dawn is now yours!\nAs long as you maintain Exalted status with the Argent Dawn, you will be able to purchase additional Chromatic Mantles. They will be made available to you immediately from any of the Dawn's quartermasters.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42.8,"y":83.7,"n":"Argent Quartermaster Lightspark","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5121":{"id":5121,"t":"High Chief Winterfall","lv":59,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Donova Snowden in Winterspring wants you to defeat High Chief Winterfall.\nHigh Chief Winterfall slain","desc":"While we still know very little about why the furbolg have been ingesting this strange substance, I do think it's best that we put a stop to it before it gets out of hand.\nThe Winterfall furbolg are not a normally aggressive tribe, and this change in their behavior leads me to think that they must be under orders from their chief. We most likely can't undo the damage that has already been done, but I think that if their leader is slain, they will not get any worse.\nHead east to Winterfall Village.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCrystal Breeze Mantle Fernpulse Jerkin Willow Band Hauberk\nExperience: 6,400\n+100 reputation with Everlook","back":"Maybe you will find out more in Winterfall Village, ‹name›.","done":"Thank you so much, ‹name›. I hope to get back to my studies without worry that I will be ambushed. Please accept this as a reward.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":31.3,"y":45.2,"n":"Donova Snowden","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"4801":{"id":4801,"t":"Frostsaber E'ko","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"3 Frostsaber E'ko Frostsaber Pride Watcher 4 % , Frostsaber Huntress 3.7 % , Frostsaber Cub 3.5 % , Frostsaber Stalker 3 % and 1 more","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Juju Flurry","back":"In Winterspring, you will fight great cats called frostsabers. These beasts possess incredible speed an' cunning. If you wish ta gain the speed a' da frostsaber, bring me da E'ko you find from dem.\nRememba, you must have the Cache of Mau'ari in your inventory if you want ta hunt for E'ko.","done":"Mau'ari can derive da juju for ‹name›... Use da Cache of Mau'ari to cast dis upon yourself or your allies.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Witch Doctor Mau'ari","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"5201":{"id":5201,"t":"Winterfall Intrusion","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rivern Frostwind wants you to slay 5 Winterfall Shaman and 5 Winterfall Ursa.\nWinterfall Shaman slain : 0/ 5\nWinterfall Ursa slain : 0/ 5","desc":"My presence goes unnoticed by most, ‹name›. However, there is an annoyance that seems firmly rooted here in Winterspring: the Winterfall furbolg.\nAlthough I have never directly attacked the furbolg, they seem crazed, fearful of anything in their path. I have watched them slay countless creatures that had the misfortune to simply be in the wrong place at the wrong time.\nI am weary of their meddling -- please, help me by fighting back. Slay the furbolg and keep them away from Frostsaber Rock.","back":"The furbolgs seem to suffer from such paranoia...","done":"I am relieved to hear that for a short moment, we will not have to worry about the Winterfall intrusion.\nYou are beginning to show your perseverance, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":49.9,"y":9.8,"n":"Rivern Frostwind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"92881":{"id":92881,"t":"The high elders request","lv":11,"min":6,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Talaanis Shadowsong in Valanaar.","desc":"The attack on both the western and eastern watchtowers are not a coincidence. Based on what you told us about what occurred at the western watchtower with that skypriest, our best guess is that the cult is trying to do something to the anchor pylons.\nPlease speak with High Elder Shadowsong. He will tell you about a lead that could prove to be promising.","done":"I have a small matter that requires just the kind of assistance that an adventurer like yourself can provide.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":76.6,"n":"Valennia Stormfist","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":76.6,"n":"Talaanis Shadowsong","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});